{
  "id": "digital_banking",
  "title": "Retail mobile banking app",
  "case_type": "digital banking",
  "scenario": "Head of Digital Channels: We want to replace our ageing mobile banking app with a new one for about two million retail customers. Customers must be able to view balances and statements, transfer money to saved payees and pay utility bills. The app should be fast and user-friendly. We ship a new feature every two weeks today and want to keep that pace. Information-security lead: Every login needs multi-factor authentication, and adding a new payee must be confirmed with a one-time password. Sessions should time out after five minutes of inactivity. We want penetration tests before every release. Compliance officer: New customers can open an account inside the app, so identity verification must follow our KYC rules, and we must keep records of every verification. Customer data must stay in India and must only be used for the purposes the customer agreed to. Operations manager: The app must be available around the clock; planned downtime is only allowed on Sunday nights. Our core banking system is twenty years old and only exposes a batch file interface that runs overnight, but balances shown in the app must always be real-time. Product owner: Marketing wants to show personalised offers in the app based on each customer's full transaction history, and every screen should work for customers with visual impairments. Customers should be able to freeze a lost debit card instantly from the app. Risk team: Transfers above a reasonable limit should need extra checks before the money leaves the account.",
